# Local operator scripts stay out of the repo, but scripts/checks holds the structural guards
# that make test-frontend and CI run, so that directory is tracked.
# note: the operator tooling (scripts/orcastra-ops.sh) and the isolated-lab tooling
# (scripts/qa-hardening/) are deliberately NOT tracked. They are kept on the operator VM, the lab
# tooling in its own local repository, so the published runbooks document procedures rather than
# telling readers to fetch a script. The OpenSearch dashboard templates and their import script
# are published by orcastra-docs (docs/assets/opensearch-dashboards/), their source of truth.
scripts/*
!scripts/checks/
# The region catalogue generator: rebuilding and verifying the catalogue needs it in the repo.
!scripts/regions/
# The local CI runner behind make ci-local: the gate before a direct push.
!scripts/ci-local.sh

# Deployment tooling for hosts outside this product (the central logging host) lives in its own
# local repository on the operator VM, never in this one.
/deploy/

# Make targets that drive operator-only tooling (local.mk, loaded by the Makefile when present)
local.mk

# Artefacts orcastra-ops.sh writes when run inside a clone
backups/
.orcastra-ops.lock/
config/
backup/
documentation/
CHANGELOG.md
.github/instructions/

# Claude Code (local AI tooling - not committed to this public repo)
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# graphify knowledge graph (local tooling, never committed)
graphify-out/
.graphifyignore

# Local-only compose override (non-secret runtime config; see the file header)
docker-compose.override.yml
